---
description: Keep Taskmark as conflict-resistant project product memory
alwaysApply: true
---

# Taskmark project memory

If a Taskmark board exists in the workspace, treat it as the source of truth for planned, in-flight, and done product work.

1. Board location:
   - One git product: `<project>/taskmark/`.
   - Multiple git products: dedicated sibling `<common>-taskmark` repository
     root. Never copy the board into product repos.
   - `REPOS.md` is local-generated and gitignored.
2. Before product work, search for a matching item. Prefer an open task/bug
   that fits; if the work is follow-up on something already shipped, append
   Prompt & feedback on that done leaf. Use `/tkmd-plan`, `/tkmd-save`,
   `/tkmd-save-do`, or `/tkmd-plan-do` only when nothing fits. Every session
   that does product work writes a `prompt` (and `feedback` when the user
   replies) row on the chosen leaf — never on `epic.md` or `story.md`.
3. Use only `/tkmd-init`, `/tkmd-verify`, `/tkmd-plan`, `/tkmd-save`,
   `/tkmd-save-do`, `/tkmd-plan-do`, `/tkmd-do`, `/tkmd-shelf`,
   `/tkmd-changelog`, `/tkmd-version`, `/tkmd-reportme`, and `/tkmd-commit`.
4. Creation writes new item files only. Never edit existing parent markdown to
   add links, rollups, logs, people, status, or dates.
5. `/tkmd-do` implements the target, never commits or pushes, never uses an
   `in_progress` stage, and marks each successfully executed leaf `done` before
   stopping. During execution, only those leaf board files may change.
6. `/tkmd-shelf` discards never-implemented work without committing or pushing.
   It writes only eligible task/bug leaves as `status: shelved`; parent markdown
   remains unchanged.
7. `/tkmd-commit` is the only user command that commits.
8. `/tkmd-changelog` writes only board-root `CHANGELOG.md`. `/tkmd-version`
   writes that changelog plus the chosen SemVer on the board `package.json`,
   every linked product-root `package.json`, and the Cursor plugin
   `plugin.json`. They never commit or write a README changelog.
   `/tkmd-reportme` writes only `.reports/report-YYYYMMDD.md` on the board,
   reporting the current git identity's done leaves since the previous report.
   That directory is local-generated and gitignored.
9. Parent hierarchy, rollups, logs, status, implementers, and lifecycle dates
   are read-time views over descendant leaves.
10. Never create or refresh `INDEX.md`, `SIZING.md`, `VELOCITY.md`, or a
    generated board dashboard README. `/tkmd-init` may create or repair the
    static project README (product-root, or `*-taskmark` board root).
    `/tkmd-verify` may delete leftover generated files and strip legacy item
    markdown. Never write a Last synced field or a README changelog.
11. Agent-written board markdown uses the board writing language stored as
    `taskmark.writingLanguage` in board `package.json` (any language chosen at
    init; default is the usual Cursor-agent language). Chat language does not
    change that. If the field is missing, use the init default. Do not
    translate existing files unless the current task explicitly rewrites them.
